# ROMs and disk images: no copy of a catalog asset belongs in this repository.
#
# app/src/main/assets/emu_avw.rom was tracked here until 2026-09-07 - 524,288
# bytes of it, in every clone and inside every APK - and it was the one file
# this app shipped that had a published, hashed counterpart and was never once
# compared against it.  Every ROM and every disk image now comes from the
# romwbw_disks interface-v0 catalog, reached through the one URL compiled in
# (INDEX_URL in data/DiskCatalogRepository.kt), and is checked against the size
# and the sha256 that only that catalog publishes before it is used -
# DiskDownloadManager.readVerifiedRom() re-hashes the ROM on every load and not
# only after the download.  A copy committed here gets none of that.  It has no
# catalog entry to be checked against, so it is not a faster copy of a published
# asset; it is an image with no claim attached, and the only way to learn that
# it is wrong is for a guest to boot to nothing.
#
# What it actually was, measured rather than assumed:
# `git show HEAD:app/src/main/assets/emu_avw.rom | sha256sum` gives
# 4b11402a29fad22de304775b7c415eb6a74600df06bd57828b9931a7e9693258, which is
# exactly the sha256 romwbw_disks publishes for emu_avw-v0-3.5.1.rom.  So it had
# NOT drifted: it was a second, byte-identical copy of a file the catalog
# already serves and already hashes.  That is the ordinary case and it is still
# the reason to refuse it.  A duplicate is only correct until the day it is not,
# it costs 512 KB in every clone and every APK to be right by luck, and nothing
# in the tree could ever have told anyone which day that was - the copy carried
# no claim, so there was nothing to check it against.  The sibling z80cpmw
# deleted the same file for the same reason in its commit 6496fd4.
# Measured 2026-09-07 against romwbw_disks catalog/v0/3.5.1/catalog.json.
#
# *.img is preventive rather than corrective: no disk image has ever been
# tracked in this repository, and the catalog serves its disks as .img.  Both
# patterns are unanchored, unlike the paths above, because no directory in this
# tree is the right home for one and naming a directory would only move the
# problem.  Nothing the build needs matches either: at the time these were added
# git ls-files listed no tracked file with either extension.
*.rom
*.img

# Log files
*.log

# Temp files
tmpclaude-*
nul
